<%- include('partials/header') %>

    <section class="page-header">
      <h1>Built for machines that can't stop to think.</h1>
      <p class="page-sub">
        Nova started with a simple observation: the machines doing the most
        useful work — sorting, hauling, inspecting — are usually the ones
        that can least afford to wait for an answer.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="prose-block">
      <p>
        We build the layer between a machine's sensors and its motors: the
        part that decides what to do next. That software has to run
        continuously, hold up when a sensor drops out, and make the safe
        call before a person ever has to intervene.
      </p>
      <p>
        Today Nova runs on fleets across warehouses, construction sites,
        and outdoor terrain — different hardware, different environments,
        the same core decision loop underneath.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="features">
      <div class="panel">
        <span class="corner tl"></span><span class="corner tr"></span>
        <span class="corner bl"></span><span class="corner br"></span>
        <span class="panel-tag">principle</span>
        <h3>Reliability first</h3>
        <p>A system that's fast but wrong isn't useful. We test for the failure cases before we ship the feature.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="panel">
        <span class="corner tl"></span><span class="corner tr"></span>
        <span class="corner bl"></span><span class="corner br"></span>
        <span class="panel-tag">principle</span>
        <h3>Built for the edge</h3>
        <p>Decisions happen on the machine, not in a data center three states away. Connectivity is a bonus, not a requirement.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="panel">
        <span class="corner tl"></span><span class="corner tr"></span>
        <span class="corner bl"></span><span class="corner br"></span>
        <span class="panel-tag">principle</span>
        <h3>Open instrumentation</h3>
        <p>Every decision a machine makes is logged and inspectable. If something goes wrong, you can see exactly why.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cta">
      <h2>Want to know how it would run on your fleet?</h2>
      <p>Tell us what you're operating and we'll show you what changes.</p>
      <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Start a conversation</a>
    </section>
